.TH COUNT_FILES 1 "October 2026" "count-files 2.0"
.SH NAME
count_files \- count regular files in a directory
.SH SYNOPSIS
count_files [\-e extension] [\-r] [\-h] [directory]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Counts regular files, directories and symbolic links in a directory
and shows the total size of the files.
If no directory is given, the directory from the config file is used,
or /etc if there is no config file.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\-e extension
Count only files with this extension, for example: \-e conf
.TP
\-r
Also count files in all subdirectories.
.TP
\-h
Show help and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
/etc/count-files.conf
Config file. The line DEFAULT_DIR=/some/dir sets the default directory.
